    narr:narration """On 2026-07-25, Quinton Fairweather issued a single recorded utterance pairing an operational commitment with a principle of capability. The commitment: [monthly Atlas rollback rehearsals](narr:Expr_1UnprotectedBaseProbe_1), effective immediately. The warrant: [an unrehearsed rollback is one you do not actually have](narr:Expr_1UnprotectedBaseProbe_2) — phrased as antithesis, plain-spoken, conviction at principle level. The [composite frame](narr:Expr_1UnprotectedBaseProbe_3) records both segments as one utterance, attributing them to Quinton and signing under Quinton as principal. Two metadata extractions by XenaExpertgh follow: the [cadence](narr:Expr_1UnprotectedBaseProbe_4) and the [owner](narr:Expr_1UnprotectedBaseProbe_5), both at decision-level conviction and legitimate-authority footing. The hub's frame — readiness constituted by rehearsal, not assertion — is carried entirely by Quinton's antithetical second sentence; the first sentence supplies the operational instantiation. The style lane is org-voiced antithesis (2 observations), concentrated in the principle statement.""" ;
